import os
D = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))), "art", "bosses", "source")
BASE = ("Original 2D game character sprite sheet for the action-survival game KYNTRAZE: FRACTURE RUSH (setting: Gloam Circuit, a fractured transit-ring under a dark night sky, floor is dark navy steel with teal circuit inlays). "
 "The reference image shows the hero's rendering style (clean dark outline, cel-shaded two-tone shading, crisp hard edges, readable at small size): match that clean cel-shaded outline style, with a consistent 3-4 px dark outline, flat shading steps, no soft gradients, no blur, no painterly noise. "
 "Seen from a slightly raised three-quarter top-down angle, body FACING RIGHT (east). Same scale in every cell, same ground/shadow reference line near the bottom of each cell, nothing cropped, character fully inside with generous margin. ")
LAY = ("Layout: EXACTLY 8 cells on flat magenta (#ff00ff) in 2 rows of 4, evenly spaced with wide magenta gutters, one pose per cell, no text, no labels, no grid lines, no ground shadows, no watermark. Wide 16:9 canvas.\n")
HEAD = BASE + "NO orange, NO gold, NO cyan anywhere. " + LAY
HEAD_H = BASE + "NO orange or gold anywhere. " + LAY
SER = ("CHARACTER: BOSS THE NULL SERAPH - a slender, elegant hovering anomaly, the opposite of a bruiser: a tall narrow robed humanoid torso of dark obsidian-violet plates (#2a1f45) with bone-white edge trim and glowing violet-white (#e6d9ff / #b98cff) energy seams, an empty faceless angular head with a single vertical violet-white slit eye, a large CRACKED HALO ring (broken into 3 angular segments) floating behind the head, and 6 long knife-shaped crystal WING-SHARDS floating in a loose fan on each side of its back (not attached), long thin arms ending in needle fingers, the lower body tapering into a hovering point with trailing ribbon-shards (no legs). About 140 px tall at final size including halo and wings; wide airy silhouette of floating shards around a thin core. Hovering about 20 px above the ground.\n")
s1 = HEAD + SER + ("ROW 1 (cells 1-4): a looping 4-frame hover cycle: gentle bob, wing-shards drifting to different positions, halo rotating slightly, arms relaxed.\n"
 "ROW 2: cell 5 = VOLLEY WIND-UP: both arms spread forward, five prism crystals forming in an arc in front of the hands, halo flared and bright, eye wide. cell 6 = VOLLEY RELEASE: arms thrust forward, crystals launched, wing-shards flung back by recoil, white flash at the hands. cell 7 = BLINK-OUT: the body dissolving into a vertical beam of light, lower half already fragmented into floating shards, semi-dissolved. cell 8 = BLINK-IN: the body re-forming from scattered shards and light, upper body solid, lower body still assembling.\n")
s2 = HEAD + SER + ("Match the exact identity, proportions, palette and scale of the second reference image (the same Seraph, sheet 1). \nROW 1: cell 1 = RING WIND-UP: arms spread wide to the sides, body upright, a ring of small energy orbs gathering around the torso, halo flared wide. cell 2 = RING RELEASE: arms thrown outward, the ring of orbs bursting outwards in all directions, wing-shards blown wide, bright flash. cell 3 = RECOVER: exhausted, drifting lower, head bowed, wing-shards drooping, seams dim - an open vulnerable pose. cell 4 = HURT: jolted back, wing-shards scattering, bright pale-violet flash edge.\n"
 "ROW 2: cell 5 = PHASE CHANGE: the Seraph unfurling at full size, arms wide, halo fully reassembled and blazing, wing-shards fanned out like a huge starburst, brighter seams - a dramatic power-up pose. cell 6 = DEATH 1: cracks of white light across the torso, halo splitting, shards drifting off. cell 7 = DEATH 2: the body breaking apart into large shards with a violet-white flash, halo broken in pieces. cell 8 = DEATH 3: only a loose cluster of fading dim shards and a few halo fragments drifting at the ground line, almost gone.\n")
open(os.path.join(D, "seraph1-prompt.txt"), "w").write(s1); open(os.path.join(D, "seraph2-prompt.txt"), "w").write(s2)
HOST = "Hostile Fracture creature family: dark gunmetal / obsidian shell plates with hot crimson-magenta (#ff3a6e) glowing energy seams, small pale-bone highlight edges. Feet/contact at the bottom of each cell on one common ground line.\n"
CH = ("ELITE AEGIS SHARDBEARER - a heavy wedge-shaped armoured warrior: broad wide shoulders, short stout legs, a small helmeted head with one crimson visor slit, carrying a LARGE upright crystalline kite-shield plate (shard-glass, crimson-edged, bone-white rim) held forward in front of its body that covers nearly half of its silhouette. Dark gunmetal / obsidian armour with crimson-magenta seams. Wider than tall, about 82 px tall at final size. Silhouette: a wedge with a big angular plate in front.\n")
aeg = HEAD_H + HOST + CH + ("ROW 1 (cells 1-4): a looping 4-frame heavy walk cycle, plate held forward, stomping steps.\nROW 2: cell 5 = RAM WIND-UP: braced low behind the plate, shoulder dug in, leaning back to charge, seams bright. cell 6 = RAM RELEASE: lunging forward at full stretch, plate thrust ahead like a battering ram, motion pose. cell 7 = HURT / SHIELD DOWN: staggered, the plate dropped and swung aside exposing the body, flash edge. cell 8 = DEATH: collapsing, plate shattering into shards in a crimson flash.\n")
CA = ("ELITE RIFT CANTOR - a thin hovering ritual caster: long draped dark robe tapering to a hovering point (no legs), narrow shoulders, long sleeves with thin hands, a faceless pointed hood with two crimson eyes, a bright thin floating HALO RING (full circle, crimson-white) vertically behind its head, and THREE long thin prong-shaped shards orbiting its torso. Dark gunmetal / obsidian robe plates with crimson-magenta and violet (#c13bff) seams and bone-white trim. More ritual and robed than a mechanical caster; clearly a different silhouette from a tall spindle with a crown: it has a big round halo and drapery. About 72 px tall at final size. Hovering about 12 px above the ground.\n")
can = HEAD_H + HOST + CA + ("ROW 1 (cells 1-4): a looping 4-frame hover-drift cycle: robe swaying, prongs at different orbit positions, halo steady.\nROW 2: cell 5 = CAST WIND-UP: arms raised and spread, prongs fanned out in front pointing forward, halo flaring bright, eyes wide. cell 6 = CAST RELEASE: arms thrust forward, three glowing orbs flying out from the prongs, recoil lean, flash. cell 7 = HURT: jolted back, prongs scattering, halo flickering, flash edge. cell 8 = DEATH: halo cracking, robe unravelling into shards in a crimson-violet flash.\n")
open(os.path.join(D, "aegis-prompt.txt"), "w").write(aeg); open(os.path.join(D, "cantor-prompt.txt"), "w").write(can)
FXH = "Game VFX sprite sheet for KYNTRAZE: FRACTURE RUSH, crisp cel-shaded with dark outline, hard stepped edges, no blur, no text, no shadows. Draw EXACTLY 4 items in a 2x2 grid on flat magenta (#ff00ff), far apart, nothing cropped, each in its own cell. Wide 16:9 canvas.\n"
f1 = FXH + ("1. PRISM BOLT: a violet-white crystalline shard projectile pointing right (east), long faceted diamond shape with a bright white core, deep violet (#7a3cff) body, thick near-black violet outline, short tail of 3 small shards behind it, about 2.4:1 aspect. Reads clearly on a dark blue floor. No orange/gold/cyan.\n2. PRISM HIT: a violet-white radial shatter burst of angular crystal shards with a white core flash, top-down, dark outline on shards.\n"
 "3. ORB BOLT: a round crimson-magenta (#ff3a6e) energy orb projectile with a white-hot core, a thick dark red outline, a small crown of 6 short spikes around it and a short fading tail behind-left. No orange.\n4. SHIELD BLOCK: a small bright pale-rose and white hexagonal spark flash: a hex outline shard-burst with 6 short rays, used when a shield blocks a hit.\n")
f2 = FXH + ("1. BLINK SIGIL: a perfectly circular (true circle, top-down, NOT a flattened ellipse) arcane ground sigil: thin double ring in violet-white (#b98cff / #f0e8ff) with a dark outline, inner ring with 8 small angular tick runes and a small inner triangle pattern, semi-translucent look, full circle centred in the cell.\n"
 "2. BLINK FLASH: a tall vertical beam of violet-white light, narrow bright core with a wider faceted glow and a few rising shard sparks, about 1:3 aspect, crisp stepped edges.\n3. AURA RING: a perfectly circular (true circle, top-down) rally aura floor ring: a thin crimson-rose ring (#ff6a8a) with small notched ticks all around and a very faint inner disc; subtle and low-contrast, no teal, no cyan.\n"
 "4. EMBLEM SERAPH: a bold square UI emblem: a cracked circular halo with a vertical slit eye in its centre and two sweeping knife-wing shapes, white-bone and violet (#b98cff) glyph on a flat dark circular badge with thin bone rim, symmetrical, icon style, readable at 32 px.\n")
open(os.path.join(D, "fx1-prompt.txt"), "w").write(f1); open(os.path.join(D, "fx2-prompt.txt"), "w").write(f2)
